sub:Head {
  this: a np:Nanopublication ;
    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/hypothesis/flying-fish-simulator-reproduces-taxi-glide-sequence> a delphi:Hypothesis, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "A point-mass model with measured fin aerodynamics reproduces a flying fish taxi-and-glide sequence, but only after post-hoc changes" ;
    dct:description "A 2D side-view model (RK4, 1 ms) of the Park and Choi 2010 specimen L3, with its measured mass, areas, lift and drag coefficients and ground effect, swims to 10 m/s, taxis with the tail in the water, lifts off at 16.5 m/s, glides 36 m in 3.1 s to 3.1 m, and repeats: six glides, 288 m in 23 s, against field figures of up to 50 m per glide at 15 to 20 m/s and 400 m in 30 s. The validation was pre-registered before the first run; the model was then changed after seeing results (taxi trim law, approach angle, breach rule, taxi thrust factor), so tests 1 to 3 are exploratory and the status of this record is inconclusive. The single glide exceeds the pure-glide bound h_max (L/D)max = 35 m by the kinetic energy gained in the taxi, which shows why long field flights need repeated taxis." ;
    delphi:context "Claim under test: thompson1917-ch02-06 (D Arcy Thompson 1917, On Growth and Form, ch. II, Project Gutenberg 55264 lines 1716-1790), with thompson1917-ch02-07 and thompson1917-ch02-10. Taxon: Exocoetidae, NCBI Taxonomy 76072, GBIF 2968. Class Aves is the frozen holdout (holdout/exam.json); no bird value enters this record." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/physics-simulator-run-6> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1242/jeb.046052>, <https://doi.org/10.3354/ab00494>, <https://doi.org/10.1088/1748-3190/ab23e6>, <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00044128> ;
    skos:scopeNote "Simulated: every number in the evidence item. Measured: the fin polar and morphometrics. Secondary: the field targets. The record is exploratory by the hub's ruling of 2026-10-31." ;
    rdfs:comment "Status: inconclusive. Does not establish: that the parameters are right (several are assumed or tuned to the very figures used as targets); that the field figures, all second-hand, are accurate; that the model generalises beyond one 60 g specimen; anything about powered flight; anything about birds. A simulation that runs proves the program executes and nothing more." ;
    rdfs:comment "Pre-registration: physics/tests/thompson1917-ch02-06/result.json, written 2026-10-31T18:21:00Z before any wing loading, lifting area or lift coefficient was read, amended 2026-10-31T18:26:00Z before any fit ran (the file lists both and the values seen before each); sha256 at build 0094c084db22278a5f98d96cc2971ccd27813b0acdc458d60cadf7c7b7bcae48. The git commit that timestamps it is pending: the physics thread does not commit; the hub does." ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch02-06> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/physics/>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/physics/results.json> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/physics-simulator-run-6> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Run 6 of the simulator, headless, with the run log" ;
    dct:description "Pre-registration physics/sim/PREREG.md (sha256 in PREREG.sha256, written 2026-10-31T20:34Z before run 1). Run log physics/sim/RUNS.md: six runs and two sweeps, every change with its reason; four deviations listed. Parameters and kinds in dashboard/public/t/physics/sim/params.json: measured (Park and Choi 2010), secondary (field figures), assumed (control law, breach rule, lobe geometry, water drag) and tuned (swim thrust to 10 m/s, taxi thrust factor 0.7 to the taxi length). Test 4, that the real fish cannot power-fly, is untouched and not run (physiology chain pending)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/hypothesis/flying-fish-simulator-reproduces-taxi-glide-sequence> ;
    rdfs:comment "Computed by physics/analysis.py from physics/glide-data.csv (sha256 bc24245b5163723b192e95fccf714ef6e4b3b28e71df4fef3befbaf008a00635) and physics/comparison-data.csv (sha256 e0d3d74639c1fe856fe5128c1783151596fde3acc923a2409be3d3f870cc394a); numbers in physics/results.json (sha256 63336841c0d4c9ae2760ae5c87a9251b97218e3ebfdd453cad4cffb9cdf6ba0b). Every input value carries its source, locator, retrieval time and value kind in those files." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/physics/results.json>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/physics/data/glide-data.csv>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/physics/data/comparison-data.csv> .
}

